[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SharpSafeNumerics requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-003
TITLE: Expected arithmetic failures
STATEMENT: Expected arithmetic failures return statuses, not exceptions.
COMMENT: Parent baseline from PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md; whole-library closure is not claimed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-007
TITLE: Explicit arithmetic policies
STATEMENT: Reject, Saturate, Wrap and Throw shall be explicit arithmetic policies.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-007-VALIDATION
TITLE: Undefined policy rejection
STATEMENT: All undefined ArithmeticPolicy byte values shall throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException for policy before arithmetic, irrespective of whether operands overflow.
COMMENT: Implementation SafeInteger.Add/Subtract/Multiply; verification PolicyValidationTests and wide arithmetic oracle campaigns.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-010
TITLE: Independent arithmetic oracles
STATEMENT: Arithmetic shall have exhaustive small-domain and independent wide-integer oracle verification.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-010-WIDE
TITLE: Wide arithmetic and policy campaign
STATEMENT: Each supported built-in integer type shall be tested against exact BigInteger arithmetic for add/subtract/multiply/divide/negate and every Add/Subtract/Multiply policy, including failure outputs, endpoints, zero/sign transitions and seeded full-width values.
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/Shared/WideIntegerOracle.cs, tests/SharpSafeNumerics.UnitTests/WideArithmeticTests.cs,
tests/SharpSafeNumerics.PropertyTests/Program.cs and tests/SharpSafeNumerics.AotSmoke/Program.cs.
Evidence: docs/verification/2026-11-17-rc1.md (qualification in progress).
Finite deterministic and randomized campaigns are evidence, not a global correctness proof.
Throw-path samples allocate intentionally.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011
TITLE: Declarative bounded domains
STATEMENT: Attributes and source generation shall provide strongly typed reflection-free bounded integer values.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-013
TITLE: Strict numeric diagnostics
STATEMENT: Roslyn diagnostics SSN1001 through SSN1008 shall enforce statically detectable numeric-safety contracts within their documented detection scope.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-010-SIMD
TITLE: Detected SIMD batch addition
STATEMENT: >>>
Signed 32-bit batch addition shall use available 256-bit and 128-bit SIMD with
scalar fallback and tails, preserving scalar exact results, error direction and
zero failure outputs per lane. Length/capacity/overlap errors shall be returned as
data before any destination write. Read-only inputs may alias; written prefixes
shall be disjoint, and unused destination suffixes shall remain untouched.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation SafeInteger.Batch.cs; verification BatchArithmeticTests against
BigInteger across width ceilings, byte-level aliases, malformed capacities and
100000-call warmed allocation checks; Native AOT/platform smoke supplies detected
dispatch evidence. Tests never force instructions absent on the executing CPU.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-004
TITLE: Supported integer domains
STATEMENT: Signed/unsigned 8-128 bits plus nint/nuint shall be supported.
COMMENT: Parent baseline from PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md; conversion is one scoped obligation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-005
TITLE: Qualified hot-path allocation
STATEMENT: Designated hot paths shall perform zero managed allocations.
COMMENT: Parent baseline from PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md; evidence must identify qualified paths/platforms.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-003-CONV
TITLE: Expected failures are data
STATEMENT: >>>
Built-in integer TryConvert shall return OutOfRange, without raising or catching
an exception for expected range rejection. Failure shall clear the output to zero.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/SharpSafeNumerics.Core/SafeInteger.cs, TryConvert.
Verification: tests/SharpSafeNumerics.UnitTests/ConversionTests.cs.
Evidence: docs/verification/2026-11-17-conversion.md (bounded conversion pass).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-004-CONV
TITLE: Built-in conversion matrix
STATEMENT: >>>
TryConvert shall preserve exactly representable values and reject all other values
for each ordered pair of byte, sbyte, short, ushort, int, uint, long, ulong,
Int128, UInt128, nint and nuint. Native widths follow the executing architecture.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: SafeInteger.TryConvert. Verification: ConversionTests matrix,
BigInteger oracle, exhaustive 8-bit sources and deterministic seed 731921.
Evidence: docs/verification/2026-11-17-conversion.md.
A finite campaign does not prove all wide integer values.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-005-CONV
TITLE: Conversion allocation budget
STATEMENT: >>>
Warmed built-in TryConvert success and range-rejection paths shall allocate zero
managed bytes in 100000 measured calls per path and type pair, excluding test
setup, assertion construction and generic instantiation warmup.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: ConversionTests.Allocation_paths over all 144 ordered type pairs.
Allocation evidence is runtime/platform-specific; no WCET or custom-provider guarantee.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-ALIASED-OUTPUT
TITLE: Bounded receiver and input preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Generic and generated bounded arithmetic shall support the receiver as its own
out destination. Generated parsers and decoders shall consume input before
publishing an overlapping result. Write and format APIs shall document that
destination and count output storage must be distinct. Batch execution metadata
shall return by value, and a default BatchArithmeticResult shall be uninitialized.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Bounded.TryAdd/TrySubtract, BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs,
SafeInteger.AddBatch and BatchArithmeticResult.
Verification: InPlaceBoundedTests, GeneratedContractTests, GeneratedDomainTests,
and BatchArithmeticTests. Evidence: docs/verification/2026-11-17-rc1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-DOC-INTERACTIVE
TITLE: Interactive CSharp capability comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
An offline HTML guide shall explain where SharpSafeNumerics adds contracts to
built-in CSharp facilities, with interactive arithmetic policy, exact conversion,
bounded domain and SIMD partition demonstrations. Browser semantic models shall
be labeled and checked against fixtures from the real package. The guide shall
preserve 128-bit integer precision and document evidence scope and limitations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: docs/interactive-deep-dive.html and eng/DeepDiveEvidence.
Verification: eng/VerifyDeepDive.cjs, eng/VerifyDeepDiveMutations.ps1,
CI fixture agreement, and docs/verification/2026-11-17-html-deep-dive.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-PACK-REPRO
TITLE: Reproducible candidate package archives
STATEMENT: >>>
With the pinned SDK, identical source/configuration, fixed package timestamp and
same build paths, repeated packaging shall produce byte-identical five NuGet
packages and three symbol archives. Verification shall compare whole-file SHA256
values, reject stale output directories and retain the tested scope. Rebuild
reproducibility shall be reported separately from repacking unchanged binaries.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Directory.Build.props DeterministicTimestamp and
eng/VerifyPackageReproducibility.ps1. Verification: local negative/positive
repacking campaign and Core CI rebuild-between-passes check; see
verification/2026-11-17-rc1-closeout.md. Cross-path/platform rebuild identity is
not established by a same-path comparison.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-QUAL-LONG-RUN
TITLE: Bounded long qualification and explicit verdict
STATEMENT: >>>
The workstation runner shall accept an eighteen-hour total budget and an
immutable source reference, retain per-step logs, preserve a results-publication
reserve and report qualification independently from successful upload. Failed,
cancelled, timed-out or missing-prerequisite checks and unexpected source changes
shall prevent a Passed verdict; budget-skipped work shall be Incomplete. Expected
rejected tool probes shall not fail an otherwise successful qualification.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Invoke-WorkstationQualification.ps1 Get-QualificationStatus,
source-integrity capture, deadline scheduler and package reproducibility step.
Verification: WorkstationRunner.Tests.ps1 (18-hour plan/verdict cases), prior
one-hour execution evidence, and rc1-closeout report. No eighteen-hour run is
claimed until the independent workstation actually executes and returns evidence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-API-SOURCE-GUARD
TITLE: Reviewed shipping API signature lists
STATEMENT: >>>
The shipping projects shall maintain source-controlled nullable-aware API
lists and reject unlisted public additions or stale signatures through build
errors. Verification shall challenge additions, member removal/rename, enum
values, optional defaults and nullability. Unpublished candidate signatures shall
remain labeled Unshipped. Scope limits including generic constraints and generated
consumer APIs shall be explicit; signature agreement is not behavioral proof.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PublicAPI.*.txt in the shipping projects,
Directory.Build.targets and Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers 5.6.0.
Verification: eng/VerifyPublicApi.ps1 and
verification/2026-11-17-api-baseline.md. SDK package validation remains a separate
compatibility layer, not replaced by these source lists.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-QUAL-COMPACT
TITLE: Native compact qualification evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
A reusable native preprocessor shall produce deterministic bounded qualification
triage reports from real workstation, numeric soak, mutation, coverage and soak
tail evidence. It shall retain exact counts, source identities, seeds, failures,
missing/corrupt evidence and explicit omission counts with raw SHA256 references.
It shall distinguish preprocessing success from qualification success, reject
contradictory success claims, preserve unknown values and independent source
scopes, and never infer success from upload or an empty input. Inputs and existing
outputs shall be preserved. Large logs shall be streamed; default directory
discovery shall avoid recursive source/build scans. Full normalized details
shall be available separately from the bounded report.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation target: eng/qualification-preprocessor and PowerShell wrapper.
Verification: Rust directed/property/negative tests, actual-schema fixtures,
native release execution, coverage, mutation and real report comparison.
Evidence requires actual execution; configured tooling alone is not closure.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-QUAL-X86
TITLE: Actual managed Windows x86 qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
Repeatable qualification shall build with the repository-selected x64 SDK and
execute required managed regression suites under an explicitly verified isolated
NET11 x86 runtime. Native-width probes shall confirm actual32-bit process behavior
before and after the suites. Test-host diagnostics shall verify the selected x86
host; successful x64 controller execution alone shall not establish x86 coverage.
Provisioned runtime archives shall match official SHA512 metadata. Supplied
runtime/cache inputs and caller environment shall be preserved. Reports shall
retain source/binary provenance, per-suite pass/fail/skip counts and explicit
failure verdicts. Managed x86 evidence shall not imply Native AOT x86 support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: eng/Invoke-X86Qualification.ps1 and eng/NativeWidthProbe.
Verification: X86Qualification.Tests.ps1, NativeWidthProbe.Tests.ps1, actual
437-case execution, native-width oracle and host diagnostics. Scope/source
evidence: verification/2026-11-17-x86.md. Windows CI runs the same helper.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-QUAL-EXPANDED
TITLE: Reproducible expanded numeric campaigns
STATEMENT: >>>
A nonshipping campaign shall accept a bounded positive duration and seed,
validate malformed or duplicate CLI options, preserve existing output files,
and retain explicit pass/fail verdicts and reproducible failure diagnostics.
Fixed arithmetic shall be checked against independent BigInteger relations;
all three safe decimal formats shall be checked against independent PeterO
arithmetic and precision-loss expectations. Generator choices shall be stable
functions of shrinkable inputs and avoid sign/exponent parity correlation.
Reports shall distinguish executed callbacks, assertions, API calls and unique
inputs; counts alone shall not establish unvisited branch coverage. Long-run
source/binary provenance and any external deadline shall be recorded separately
from shorter campaigns or changed report-serialization implementations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: tests/SharpSafeNumerics.NumericSoak. Verification:
NumericSoakRunner.Tests.ps1, deterministic distribution checks, disposable
oracle-fault shrinking control, scoped coverage and managed/native short runs.
Evidence: verification/2026-11-17-numeric-soak-harness.md and the final bounded
qualification report. Actual long-run success remains pending until observed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-017
TITLE: Referenced SharpUnits integration example
STATEMENT: >>>
A reproducible example shall compile against real immutable SharpUnits source
and bridge initialized whole-volt bounded values into coherent SI voltage
quantities. Its contiguous integer domain shall be restricted to minus through
plus two to the power 53, preserving every admitted magnitude exactly through
the upstream double interface. Invalid default/domain values shall reject with
cleared output. Verification shall check actual electrical dimensions and
boundary rejection. Unit display metadata alone shall not count as integration.
Core shall not acquire a SharpUnits runtime dependency. General exact unit
arithmetic and compatibility with an unpublished NuGet release are not implied.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Stable product requirement SN-017, previously recorded in PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md.
Implementation: examples/SharpUnitsInterop and eng/VerifySharpUnitsIntegration.ps1.
Upstream pin: 7ebdbcda9958e4eb4cee623065ecdd37395dac89. Verification: source
integration assertions seed731931, script negative controls and recorded
managed/native execution. Evidence: verification/2026-11-17-sharpunits.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-018
TITLE: Fixed-point semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
The package shall provide owned fixed-point arithmetic with documented scale,
rounding, representability and expected-failure behavior. The RC1 implementation
scope shall be the signed Q32.32 contract specified by SN-018-FIXED.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Stable product ID imported from PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md. The user included this
feature in RC1 on 2026-11-17. Verification evidence and limits are recorded in
verification/2026-11-17-fixed-decimal.md; arbitrary fixed-point formats are not
implied by the scoped implementation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-018-FIXED
TITLE: Owned signed Q32.32 arithmetic
STATEMENT: >>>
Fixed64 shall represent a signed Int64 raw value divided by two to the power 32.
SafeFixed shall provide raw admission, integral and rational conversion, addition,
subtraction, multiplication, division and negation without silent saturation or
wrapping. Widened intermediates shall prevent premature overflow. Exact rounding
shall reject discarded fractions; explicit nearest-even, toward-zero, floor,
ceiling and away-from-zero modes shall define signed rounding. Undefined modes
shall reject before operand-dependent success or failure. Expected failures shall
return statuses and cleared result storage. Default Fixed64 is valid zero;
default NumericResult is invalid. Strict integer and fixed arithmetic shall not
use runtime reflection or BigInteger intermediates.
Exact fractional rejection shall precede range validation; other rounding shall
precede range validation and may admit a value rounded back to an endpoint.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Parent product requirement: SN-018. User-authorized RC1 scope expansion on
2026-11-17. Implementation: Core/Fixed64.cs (including SafeFixed),
Fixed64Tests.cs, PropertyTests/Program.cs, formal/FixedPoint.dfy.
Independent reference: test-only exact BigInteger rationals with retained seeds.
The formal model is not a refinement proof of the handwritten CSharp code.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019
TITLE: Safe Decimal32 Decimal64 and Decimal128 operations
STATEMENT: >>>
The package shall provide explicit safety contracts around NET11 built-in IEEE
Decimal32, Decimal64 and Decimal128 finite arithmetic and conversion, including
special-value admission and precision-loss handling, as specified by
SN-019-DECIMAL. The optional implementation shall not widen the strict integer
allocation contract to include decimal exactness checking.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Stable product ID imported from PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md. The user approved safe
wrappers over the built-in decimal engine on 2026-11-17. This scoped requirement
does not assert whole IEEE754 operation/status/encoding conformance.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-DECIMAL
TITLE: Safe built-in IEEE decimal arithmetic
STATEMENT: >>>
The optional Decimal assembly shall wrap NET11 System.Numerics.Decimal32,
Decimal64 and Decimal128 for finite addition, subtraction, multiplication,
division, negation and cross-format conversion. Exact is the default rounding
contract and rejects unrepresentable exact results. Explicit nearest-even may
accept rounded finite results and shall report inexactness. Nonfinite operands,
division by zero, nonfinite overflow results, unsupported numeric types and
undefined rounding modes shall return typed failures with cleared output.
Undefined modes shall reject before operand-dependent paths. Exactness shall be
determined using exact rational relations, not rounded reverse-operation tests.
Default result shall be invalid. Decimal exactness checking may allocate and is
outside the allocation-free strict integer contract. No whole IEEE754 operation
set, arbitrary rounding modes or transcendental conformance is implied.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Parent product requirement: SN-019. User-authorized RC1 scope expansion on
2026-11-17. Implementation: SharpSafeNumerics.Decimal. Independent
verification: PeterO.Numbers 1.8.2 in tests only, rational references, malformed
options, boundary/subnormal/conversion cases, coverage, mutation and Native AOT.
Closure requires executed evidence; the existing pinned integer soak does not
qualify these newly added operations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-CONTEXT
TITLE: Explicit IEEE decimal rounding and exception context
STATEMENT: >>>
The optional decimal package shall provide an IEEE operation API for Decimal32,
Decimal64 and Decimal128 independently of the finite-only SafeDecimal contract.
Each call shall take explicit nearest-even, nearest-away, toward-zero,
toward-negative or toward-positive rounding and optional trap flags. Invalid,
divisionByZero, overflow, underflow and inexact shall be independent flags.
IEEE NaN and infinity results shall remain available unless trapped; invalid
types/options shall fail before operand-dependent paths with cleared storage.
Decimal tininess shall be detected before rounding. Default result is invalid;
default context is nearest-even without traps. No ambient process state changes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
User-authorized expansion 2026-11-18. Implementation: IeeeDecimalContracts.cs,
IeeeDecimalArithmetic.cs. Existing SN-019-DECIMAL remains the compatible finite
API contract. IEEE exceptions are not the directional SafeDecimal range errors.
Evidence: independent arithmetic oracles and applicable GDA corpus; full closure
requires the operation-specific matrix, not an API-presence assertion.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-REPRESENTATION
TITLE: IEEE decimal representations and predicates
STATEMENT: >>>
The IEEE API shall preserve signed zeros, cohorts and NaN sign/signaling/payload
where required by the selected operation. It shall provide BID/DPD interchange,
classification, all required quiet/signaling Boolean comparison predicates,
totalOrder, totalOrderMag, quantum, adjacent values, decimal scaling, integral
rounding, invariant parsing/formatting and payload operations. Invalid syntax
shall not produce a numeric value. Valid extreme decimal exponents shall round
by value rather than fail solely because the exponent exceeds Int32.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: IeeeDecimalCodec.cs, IeeeDecimalRepresentation.cs,
IeeeDecimalPredicates.cs. Verification: raw-pattern tests, predicate truth/flag
tables, cohort/sign cases, malformed input, payload and extreme exponent tests.
NaN payload narrowing policies for mixed conversions are explicit library choices.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-CONVERSIONS
TITLE: Exact-source mixed numeric conversion
STATEMENT: >>>
Integer and binary Half/Single/Double conversions shall use exact source values
and one final destination rounding, with flags, trap behavior and unsupported
carrier validation. Integer invalid conversion shall return the documented
selected integer zero plus Invalid unless trapped. Binary tininess selection
shall be documented separately from decimal tininess. Exact and non-exact
integer conversion shall differ in their Inexact signaling contract.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: IeeeDecimalConversions.cs. Independent verification includes
all 65536 Half encodings, integer/binary boundaries, exact rational and PeterO
references, flags, payloads and every rounding direction.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-FUNCTIONS
TITLE: Recommended IEEE decimal elementary operations
STATEMENT: >>>
The decimal API shall provide the recommended elementary functions in the
IEEE754-2019 operation matrix with explicit rounding, flags, special-value
domains, exact identities and preferred exponents. Fused definitions shall not
round an intermediate destination value. Approximate BCL forwarding or a fixed
guard-digit count alone shall not establish correctly rounded behavior.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: DecimalIntervalMath.cs, IeeeDecimalFunctions.cs,
IeeeDecimalPiFunctions.cs. Outward interval refinement certifies unique final
rounding for non-exact elementary results; exact identities are handled directly.
Finite reference sweeps and source review are not a global formal proof.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-REDUCTIONS
TITLE: IEEE extrema and exact decimal reductions
STATEMENT: >>>
All eight IEEE754-2019 extrema variants shall implement their distinct NaN,
signed-zero and magnitude-tie rules. Sum, sumAbs, sumSquare and dot shall use
exact accumulation and one final rounding. Scaled product, product-of-sums and
product-of-differences shall return a normalized source-format fraction and an
explicit integer scale without premature destination exponent overflow.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: IeeeDecimalReductions.cs. Exact accumulation is this binding's
documented accuracy choice. IEEE9.5 augmented arithmetic recommendations are
binary-format operations and are not asserted as decimal mandates.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-ENVIRONMENT
TITLE: Explicit immutable IEEE mode and status snapshots
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall provide validated explicit state snapshots for decimal and
binary destination rounding directions, traps and sticky flags, with save,
restore, raise, lower and test operations. Defaulting/restoring modes shall
preserve sticky flags. Failed validation shall not publish partial state.
These bindings shall not change the host hardware, thread or process floating
point environment or claim host-language IEEE conformance.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: IeeeDecimalEnvironment.cs. Explicit state provides composable
library behavior; IEEE host environment/version predicates remain outside the
package's conformance claim, as recorded in IEEE_DECIMAL_OPERATION_MATRIX.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-019-IEEE-QUALIFICATION
TITLE: Reproducible independent IEEE decimal verification
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualification shall retain source/run provenance, applicable independent
reference versions and licenses, actual pass/fail/skip counts, reproducible
seeds, measured line/branch coverage, mutation outcomes and known exclusions.
Malformed or unreadable corpus inputs shall not count as passing evidence.
Required/recommended decimal operations, binary-only recommendations and
host-environment claims shall remain distinguished. Verification tools and
corpora shall not become runtime arithmetic dependencies.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: eng/DecimalConformance, IEEE-specific tests, Native AOT smoke and
CI. Formal model: formal/DecimalRounding.dfy proves coefficient rounding properties;
eng/VerifyDecimalRoundingModel.ps1 verifies, emits CSharp and executes that model.
This is not a refinement proof of the handwritten CLR implementation or a
global proof of elementary-function correctness. Raw artifacts stay outside Git;
bounded reports, fixtures/provenance, helper source and reproduction steps stay in Git.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-020-WEEK-QUALIFICATION
TITLE: Unattended evolving-source IEEE decimal qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
The nonshipping qualification tooling shall support a configurable duration,
default168 hours, with bounded reproducible chunks exercising IEEE decimal32,
decimal64 and decimal128 in all five rounding directions against independent
references. Counterexamples shall retain seed, operands, operation, mode and
source identity. Inconclusive oracle comparisons shall be recorded separately
and shall not produce a fully passing campaign verdict.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
User-requested2026-11-18. Reuse existing CsCheck/PeterO test-only dependencies
and workstation process/tool/Git helpers. Production dependencies remain BCL-only.
Implementation: tests/SharpSafeNumerics.IeeeSoak and eng/Invoke-WeekQualification.ps1.
Verification: dedicated harness tests, short executed campaigns, Pester control
flow/negative tests and native preprocessor schema/property tests. A short smoke
cannot establish week-long endurance; actual future reports provide that evidence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-020-DAILY-REFRESH
TITLE: Daily source updates and immutable per-revision evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
At configurable reporting boundaries, default24 hours, the runner shall fetch
the configured source branch, resolve an exact commit and validate a fresh
isolated snapshot before activation. A chunk's source shall remain immutable.
Evidence shall remain separated by source revision. A failed update shall be
reported explicitly; continued use of the last working snapshot shall not hide
the failure or produce a fully passing overall verdict. Pinned mode shall remain
available and the orchestration runner's own version shall be recorded.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-020-WEEK-QUALIFICATION

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-020-DAILY-REPORTS
TITLE: Daily automatic results publication and recoverable execution
STATEMENT: >>>
The runner shall publish bounded daily, failure and final reports to one unique
issue-associated results branch without routine interaction. Reports shall retain
source/runner provenance, counts, seeds, failures, timings and artifact references.
Logs and checkpoints shall support diagnosis and resumption without silently
repeating seeds, overwriting existing evidence or extending the original deadline.
Failed uploads shall retain local data for retry and shall not be called submitted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-020-WEEK-QUALIFICATION

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-020-VERIFIED-CLEANUP
TITLE: Delete only owned results verified as uploaded
STATEMENT: >>>
After verifying remote commit identity and exact uploaded file contents, the
runner shall delete corresponding explicitly owned local result copies by
default. Unsubmitted data shall remain available for retry. Cleanup shall reject
out-of-root paths, reparse traversal, changed contents and foreign ownership.
It shall preserve source, checkouts, tools and unrelated files. References or
hashes alone shall not qualify unuploaded raw logs for deletion. KeepResults
shall allow retaining submitted local copies.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-020-WEEK-QUALIFICATION
